The noise fields baked by grass_noise.rs are original procedural value noise at
ao-vk's field frequencies. Native terrain samples are evaluated at runtime solely
to blend the new vegetation with the installed scene; they are not copied into
any generated texture.

Soft sun-shadow filter
======================

The blocker-search and Vogel-disk penumbra filter in
crates/ao-render/src/sun_shadows.wgsl follows the algorithm of
`CascadeVisibility` in ao-vk (https://github.com/wannabuh/ao-vk,
rvk/shaders/ffp_main.glsl), MIT licensed. The WGSL is an independent
reimplementation of the algorithm, not copied source.

HDR tonemap, grade and dither
======================

The highlight knee, sunlit-warm / shade-cool chroma grade and interleaved-gradient
dither in crates/ao-render/src/grade.wgsl follow the approach of `tonemap.frag`
(`Grade()`, `Dither8`) in ao-vk (https://github.com/wannabuh/ao-vk), MIT licensed.
The WGSL is an independent reimplementation: the tone curve, the luminance-preserving
grade and the sun-weight gating are original to this project.

The half-resolution contact-shadow march, depth-aware blur and upsample in
crates/ao-render/src/contact_shadows.{rs,wgsl} follow the algorithm of
`rvk/shaders/contact.frag` and `ao_blur.frag` in ao-vk
(https://github.com/wannabuh/ao-vk), MIT licensed. The WGSL is an independent
reimplementation of the algorithm, not copied source.

Bloom pyramid
======

The 13-tap Karis-weighted first downsample and 3x3-tent upsample chain in
crates/ao-render/src/bloom.wgsl follow the structure of rvk/shaders/bloom_down.frag
and rvk/shaders/bloom_up.frag in ao-vk (https://github.com/wannabuh/ao-vk), MIT
licensed, including its soft-knee threshold above white. The WGSL is an independent
reimplementation; the energy-preserving level mix, authored-emission seeds and
HDR tonemap interaction are specific to this renderer.
=======
Enhanced ambient occlusion sampling
===================================

The per-pixel rotated direction set, step jitter (interleaved gradient noise) and
sum/(directions*steps) normalisation in crates/ao-render/src/ambient_occlusion.wgsl
follow rvk/shaders/ao.frag and ao_blur.frag from ao-vk
(https://github.com/wannabuh/ao-vk, MIT License). The algorithm was re-expressed in
WGSL for this project's depth-bilateral pipeline; no source text or assets are copied.

Enhanced atmosphere: ao-vk
==========================

The optional height/land haze, valley mist, volumetric shafts, cloud-gap shafts,
volumetric clouds, cloud shadows and sky-disc effects adapt the atmosphere
algorithms in ao-vk (https://github.com/wannabuh/ao-vk), inspected at
53b6881eccd80b6d5887826106644ae7e7de3a44. Sources include
rvk/shaders/volume.frag, cloud_layer.frag, cloud_resolve.frag,
cloud_shadow.frag, cloud_shadow_common.glsl, cloud_light.glsl and sun.frag.
Scene inputs and visibility constraints are specific to this renderer; no
ao-vk artwork or binary assets are redistributed.
